SUMMARY:Music of the South American Baroque
DESCRIPTION:Come enjoy an afternoon showcasing the rich and diverse musical heritage of Baroque composers who lived and worked in South America\, including both European immigrants and the first generation of South American-born composers. Many of these works\, preserved in small manuscript collections in South American archives and cathedrals\, are only now becoming accessible beyond their countries of origin. \nLearn about the culture and heritage before you hear the music! A lecture will precede the concert at 3 PM \nTickets:\n$20 General\, $15 Senior\, $5 Student\, or Pay What You Can \n​Need accommodations? Contact us at info@raleighcamerata.com and let us know how we can help you enjoy our concerts!
URL:https://unitedarts.org/calendar/music-of-the-south-american-baroque/
LOCATION:Christ the King Lutheran Church\, 600 Walnut St\, Cary\, NC\, 27511
CATEGORIES:Concert
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://unitedarts.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/music-of-the-spanish-baroque-cropped_orig.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Raleigh Camerata":MAILTO:info@raleighcamerata.com
END:VEVENT
